# Issue #1021 (and #709's literal acceptance criterion): a parenthesized group whose FIRST token is
# a zero-arity reporter is a `parenthesized-expression` (grammar.md:213), not a `parenthesized-call`
# (grammar.md:215) — `==` is not an `expression`, so the call production has no derivation here at
# all, and the reader must not commit to one on the head token alone.
#
# `pi` is the head throughout because it is the exact shape #709/#1021 reported: a zero-arity Core
# reporter, whose arity this deliberately profile-blind reader never consults. Every binary operator
# of grammar.md:181-190 is swept, `-` included. Executed rather than parse-only on purpose —
# "parses clean" would not prove the group MEANS what it says, and a silent misreading is worse than
# a diagnostic. Each value below is what the same line yields with the parentheses removed, because
# grouping an expression more explicitly must never be what breaks a learner's program.
define yes
  return true
end
print (pi == pi)
print (pi != pi)
print (pi + 0)
print (pi - pi)
print (pi * 0)
print (pi / pi)
print (pi > 3)
print (pi < 4)
print (pi >= 3)
print (pi <= 4)
print (pi mod pi)
print (pi is a "number")
print (yes and false)
print (yes or true)
